  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Evidence for Migration Analysis and Policy (REMAP) - Asia and the Middle East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Action is to strengthen evidence-based formulation and implementation of humanitarian and development policy and programming on migration and forced displacement in Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Iran, Iraq, and Pakistan. In particular, IOM will contributeby gathering, analysing and sharing data on relevant topics to inform and strengthen policy and programming. This will include insight into reintegration challenges and efforts, return intentions and host/return community perceptions in relevant locations, supporting government, humanitarian, and development stakeholders (including relevant departments within IOM) to design, implement and adapt well-evidenced programming to foster resilience and self-reliance. IOM will also aim toincrease the availability and quality of information on the locations, numbers, needs and vulnerabilities of these groups, and by responsible sharing of this information with organizations and government institutions mandated and able to assist these groups and individuals.</narrative>
  </description>
